2026-11-13 21:50 Also found (for the dispatcher to file, skilletor board): (1) Skilletor::JSON::js_parse is quadratic: _string/_number copy the whole input (my $s = $p->{s}) on every call; a 221 KB file parses in ~22 s, config-oracle.json (89 KB) in 2.5 s. t/14-toml.t reads its oracle with JSON::MaybeXS for that reason. (2) Frontmatter.pm divergence: a surrogate pair written as two escapes ("\uD83D\uDE00") stays two lone surrogates in Perl (written as two U+FFFD), TS joins them into one code point; shows in a Codex agent description and the briefing line. Fix in _unescape_double. (3) TS oddity in frontmatter.ts: a __proto__ key never becomes an own key (prototype setter), so codex: {__proto__: x} vanishes and a top-level __proto__: {description: inherited} makes the agent's description 'inherited'; Perl keeps it as a plain key. k144-style TS fix, then Perl follows. (4) TS oddity mirrored in Convert.pm (%INHERITED): convert.ts asks 'key in top'/'key in tables', so a codex table named constructor, toString, valueOf, hasOwnProperty ... is dropped as a collision; Object.hasOwn in TS would let Perl drop the list. (5) Engine.pm keeps its own RULES_FILE constant; k184 can import it from Skilletor::AgentsMD.

